      "name": "Concept · Foundation · Time clock · 1440",
      "theme": {
        "mode": "light"
      },
      "width": 1440,
      "fill": "$color-surface-background",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 48,
      "padding": 64,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "LludY",
          "name": "Intro",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 8,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "vpMLf",
              "name": "Eyebrow",
              "fill": "$color-interactive",
              "content": "NEW CONCEPT · FOUNDATION · BATCH 12 · APPROVED 2026-10-20",
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-small",
              "fontWeight": "600",
              "letterSpacing": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "O9oxBn",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$color-heading",
              "content": "Time clock",
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-jumbo",
              "fontWeight": "700",
              "letterSpacing": -0.8
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "o5BmC3",
              "name": "Lead",
              "fill": "$color-text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 960,
              "content": "The work timer a crew member starts on a visit or an assessment: the ticking time, the running clock, Start and Stop, and the panel that says the timer is already running on another job. Approved by Jafar 2026-10-20. Everything they do today stays (one timer at a time, amber after 12 hours, Start pauses the day clock); nothing new is added.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-large",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "YL20k",
          "name": "Time clock · approved",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 16,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "PEvEy",
              "name": "Heading",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 4,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "O8hRfe",
                  "name": "Title",
                  "fill": "$color-heading",
                  "content": "Time clock · approved",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-family",
                  "fontSize": "$font-size-larger",
                  "fontWeight": "700",
                  "letterSpacing": -0.3
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "iiFxs",
                  "name": "Desc",
                  "fill": "$color-text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 960,
                  "content": "Timers belong to the Time part of the app, so they take its indigo. Other people's timers show as an indigo clock capsule; Start and Stop are small white buttons with indigo icons; while your timer runs, the panel turns white with an indigo edge and the time is its big number; on today's visit row the indigo-edged clock joins straight onto Stop timer. Amber after 12 hours.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.45,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-family",
                  "fontSize": "$font-size-base",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "Lz0sq",
              "name": "Panel",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "fill": "$color-surface",
              "cornerRadius": "$radius-large",
              "stroke": "$color-border",
              "strokeWidth": 1,
              "layout": "vertical",
