      "children": [
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "oOWvF",
          "name": "Intro",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 12,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Vk0dF",
              "name": "Eyebrow",
              "fill": "$color-interactive",
              "content": "NEW CONCEPT · BATCH 43 · MERGE CLIENTS POP-UP · APPROVED A · 2026-10-21",
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-small",
              "fontWeight": "600",
              "letterSpacing": 0.8
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Zq9UV",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$color-heading",
              "content": "Merge clients pop-up",
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-jumbo",
              "fontWeight": "700",
              "letterSpacing": -0.8
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "fIFlf",
              "name": "Lead",
              "fill": "$color-text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Approved by Jafar 2026-10-21: A · From → To (B form beside a summary deleted). clients/ClientMergeDialog, opened from a client page's ⋯ menu (that client starts as the one to keep). Same steps, words and checks as the live app, following Jobber's Merge client: pick the client to keep and the duplicate, Swap them, read what moves and any warnings, then Merge clients (red, because the duplicate is deleted and it can't be undone). Nothing added or removed; the counts, warnings and blockers come from the database's own preview. The duplicate (red top) sits left, the client to keep (sand top) right, an arrow between; what moves shows as record tiles in their own colours.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-large",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
