              "content": "CONCEPT · BATCH 60 · PIPELINE",
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-small",
              "fontWeight": "600",
              "letterSpacing": 0.8
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "E1ldi",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$color-heading",
              "content": "Days-in-stage chip",
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-jumbo",
              "fontWeight": "700",
              "letterSpacing": -0.6
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "owhR5",
              "name": "Lead",
              "fill": "$color-text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1100,
              "content": "Approved B by Jafar 2026-10-22; option A (grey clock pill) deleted. pipeline/StageAgeChip: how long a request or quote has sat in its current Pipeline stage. It shows on every Pipeline card (footer, beside the owner), in the Pipeline table's age column, and in the Brief drawer's status line. Same behaviour as the live app: under an hour reads 0h, then hours (7h), then whole days (21d); a screen reader hears the full sentence (“In this stage for 21 days”). Age alone never colours anything: the separate red “No progress for 12 days” warning does that, so the chip stays quiet even on an old card. Research: Pipedrive and HubSpot keep time-in-stage as a quiet fact and colour only stale deals (Pipedrive's red rotting card, HubSpot's greyed card).",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-base",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "wh6WI",
          "name": "Option B",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 20,
          "children": [
